## Another version

Each demo version is an immutable artifact, addressable by digest. To move to
one, pull it into a fresh directory and start that:

```sh
docker compose down                     # in the old directory
mkdir ../pacto-demo-next && cd ../pacto-demo-next
oras pull {{.ArtifactRepo}}:<version>
docker compose up -d --wait
```

The two directories are independent: Compose names a project after the directory
it runs in, so each version gets its own containers and its own volumes. Keeping
the old directory lets you go back to it exactly as you left it; `docker compose
down -v` in it releases its volumes when you are done.

To run both at once, give the second one ports of its own — see above.

## Credentials

There are none in this artifact. The Evidence Server generates its own signing
keypair the first time it starts and keeps it in a volume, so the demo signs as
an identity that only ever existed on your machine.

## Provenance

This artifact was built from `{{.Source}}` at version `{{.Version}}`, and runs
`{{.PactoImage}}`. The demo is a projection of the same canonical scenario
Pacto's Kubernetes acceptance suite runs against a real cluster: the same
services, revisions, dependency edge, observation source and signed evidence.
The one thing missing here is the operational targets a Kubernetes controller
reconciles — Compose has no controller, so no workload is claimed to be running.
